# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/

# Environment variables (but keep example files as templates)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test coverage
coverage/

# SQLite database — local state, never source. A pattern without a leading
# slash matches at any depth, so this covers apps/api/data/neuron.db too.
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Editor directories
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Worker artifacts — prompts and reports stay local, not in version control
docs/workers/
docs/learning/**/report.md
docs/learning/**/worker-report-*.md

# DECIDED ON DAY 14, 2026-10-02. The rule above keeps its place, and the
# Phase 1 reports stay local. They were read before this was decided and hold
# no secrets, so the reason is editorial rather than cautious: 2,649 lines of
# worker reports and 1,954 of prompts are agent output, and a reader meeting
# them before the ADRs gets a worse account of this project rather than a
# fuller one. docs/handbook/ now carries the same material in 398 lines, which
# is what the constitution actually asked for when it promised a handbook.
#
# The exceptions below stay. They are learning records rather than worker
# artifacts — evidence that a named debt was repaid, which the roadmap,
# master-state and HANDOFF all point at — and that is a different kind of
# document from an implementation report.
#
# Nothing is lost: every report is still on disk and in no way deleted. If a
# future day needs one in the repository, un-ignore that file and say why.
!docs/learning/day-08/report.md
!docs/learning/day-09/report.md
!docs/learning/day-10/report.md
!docs/learning/day-11/report.md
